# Registry preference is machine-local, not a repository property.
#
# A repo-level `registry=` line is read by every command run in this directory,
# including `npm publish` — pointing it at a read-only mirror (npmmirror) makes
# publishing either fail or silently target the wrong place, and it drags every
# CI runner onto that mirror too. The publish target is therefore pinned in
# package.json -> publishConfig.registry instead, where it cannot be shadowed.
#
# Want the China mirror for installs on this machine? Set it where it belongs:
#   npm config set registry https://registry.npmmirror.com --location=user
#
# `strict-peer-dependencies` is left at its default (strict) on purpose: relaxing
# it in the repository hides real peer conflicts until they reach a user.
